Marvel Studios is apparently taking a  bit of a breather this summer pressing  pause on its production schedule after  wrapping up phase 3 of the Marvel  Cinematic Universe the slowdown seems  set to start after the launches of  Avengers endgame in April and spider-man  far from home in July taking to Twitter  in late February Deadpool co-creator Rob  Liefeld offered an intriguing  observation about where he thinks the  MCU is heading beyond 2019 as the writer  and artist pointed out after endgame and  far from home it looks as though it will  be about a year before another Marvel  film is rolled out into theaters as  Liefeld wrote in a Twitter post still  wrapping my head around the fact that  there are no Marvel movies currently  filming so a full-year absent Marvel  films following spider-man after far  from home makes its debut the next  scheduled release date for Marvel's  studio film is May 1st 2020 and as of  the start of March 2019 it's not  publicly known what that movie is going  to be whatever it is that leaves roughly  10 months between the spider-man sequel  and Marvel's mystery project prolific  comic book writer Mark Miller the writer  behind influential properties like  wanted kick-ass &amp; Kingsman the Secret  Service joined in on the conversation on  Twitter replying to Liefeld's original  tweet with his own thoughts  the writer noted that this might be the  first time in over ten years that  there's been this wide of a gap between  MCU releases he also argues that it's a  good thing calling the apparent cool  down quote a wise move he explained this  take further by writing they felt  relentless for a while and a wee wait  will only build anticipation what's  weirder is we're still not entirely sure  what's coming while Miller has never  been too closely involved with Marvel on  the moviemaking side he's no stranger to  working with the company's characters  having written four such series as  ultimate Fantastic Four ultimate x-men  and Marvel Knights spider-man among  others so while he does possess some  insider insight he seems to be as in the  dark about Marvel Studios specific plans  as any other fan in 2014 Marvel Studios  released a massive roadmap for the next  few years of MCU content culminating in  the two-part infinity war and the since  scrapped inhuman  movie now that we're reaching the end of  that sequence the future of the series  feels more unknown than ever the secrecy  makes sense it's been pointed out that  revealing the MCU future plans before  endgames release could potentially spoil  the events of endgame especially if that  climactic movie kills off an Avenger or  two for good with that in mind the  studio plane thinks close to the vest is  understandable and there are probably  some benefits to a short hiatus - while  superhero fatigue hasn't kicked in with  audiences yet it remains a real  possibility and Marvel could be wise to  take a moment after endgame to enjoy a  victory lap before getting audiences  excited for its next few dozen movies  for over a decade now the studio has  been cranking out films at a blistering  pace kicking off the MC use first phase  with six movies in the span of four  years for Phase two and beyond the  company picked up the pace seemingly  pushing its luck by bringing out as many  as three movies in one year that's what  happened in 2018 when fans were treated  to Black Panther Avengers infinity war  and ant-man and the wasp whether the  series has taken us to space other  dimensions unknown countries or the  microscopic quantum realm it's all been  accelerating toward endgame which has  been described as a conclusion of sorts  to the MCU staggering story arc about  the all-powerful Infinity stones that  Thanos has been inside my head for six  years that story ending should provide a  natural reason to put things on pause  maybe just to take a second and count  all the money the series has made  considering the 2 billion dollar  box-office performance of Avengers  infinity war which you may recall ended  in a devastating cliffhanger it's all  but guaranteed that the fourth Avengers  will be among the biggest releases of  all time capping off a decade plus of  unprecedented runaway success the Spider  Man sequel taking the webslinger out of  America for the first time for a  European tour with Mysterio also seems  poised to do big numbers so 2020 looks  like the perfect time for Marvel to  scale things back for a little bit allow  it both creators and fans time to catch  their breath and get excited again for  new stories to come while the specifics  are still unknown to the public Marvel  Studios head honcho Kevin Feige has  offered a few general teasers for the  upcoming fourth phase of the MCU  speaking to collider during a Captain  Marvel press junket Feige teased the  all-new all-different future of the  series telling viewers to definitely  expect more obscure comic characters to  get pulled off the company's deep bench  for the feature film treatment as the  producer put it  everything after endgame and after  spider-man far from home will be  different and be unique as we try to  make every film seen returning  characters is certainly something we're  going to do and want to do but also  introducing characters that the majority  of the world has never heard of much  like guardians of the galaxy much like  Avengers before we made Avengers and  there are lots of them he continued  sharing that the film about the Eternals  is in the pipeline for the post endgame  MCU that movie he says will introduce a  whole new group of legendary heroes to  the MCU at once  Feige said we like the idea of doing an  ensemble movie from the start as opposed  to building up as we did with the first  Avengers more like guardians not totally  but in terms of introducing a new group  of people he also left open the  possibility for a movie with epic scope  taking audiences far back into the past  of the MCU saying Jack Kirby did an  immense amazing epic with eternals that  spans tens of thousands of years and  that's also something we haven't really  done which is why that among many other  things post endgame we find appealing  while Marvel may be taking a short pause  from theatrical releases we can still  expect new content in an intriguing move  the studio is developing several  television series set in the MCU to  launch on Disney's upcoming streaming  platform Disney Plus unlike the Netflix  or ABC series which are produced by  Marvel television these shows will be  full-fledged Marvel Studios productions  featuring movie characters and sporting  big budgets the series lineup includes a  show about Tom Hiddleston's trickster  god Loki which is expected to premiere  later in 2019 also reportedly in the  works are a team-up series with Falcon  in the Winter Soldier and another  project centering on vision and Scarlet  Witch rumor has it that there may even  be a project in the pipeline centering  on Clint Barton's Hawkeye training Kate  bishop his eagle-eyed successor so rest  easy true believers work  more Marvel content than we know what to  do with all it's going to take is just a  little bit of patience there are some  movies we know the company is working on  including eternals Black Widow and  sequels the Black Panther Doctor Strange  and the guardians of the galaxy but when  these movies will officially appear is  still up in the air but Feige has  assured fans that the company has a  slate of movies ready to go all the way  up through 2025 who could we be seen in  the future miss Marvel the Thunderbolts  or could we soon start seeing Marvel  Studios take on x-men and the Fantastic  Four the possibilities feel limitless  but before we can get to all of that  we've got business to take care of with  Thanos it may be the end of an era but  it's also the start of something new  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff or coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

